WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:05.170
They've long since cemented themselves as
beloved pop culture icons, but what do we

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:08.800
really know about Jay and his longtime companion
Silent Bob?

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:14.230
We've compiled an exhaustive timeline of the
lives, loves, trials and good fortunes of

00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:15.920
this foulmouthed dynamic duo.

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:21.180
If you're wondering where the story of Jay
and Silent Bob begins, it might be best to

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:24.280
start with Genesis — the book of the Bible,
not the band.

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:30.280
Yes, the biblical story of creation is canon
within Kevin Smith's universe, and it's more

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:31.640
relevant than you might think.

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:37.640
As outlined in Dogma, the stories of the Bible
hold literal sway in the View Askewniverse,

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:42.190
with Biblical figures — including God herself
— showing up to influence the events of

00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:44.280
the world — and also to kill people.

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:50.080
In the beginning, God created all that is,
developed an unknowable plan for existence,

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:52.260
and looked suspiciously like Alanis Morissette.

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:56.820
While a lot of the events depicted in the
holy texts are presented as subjective and

00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:01.580
even misleading, turns out the story was,
in broad strokes, pretty accurate.

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:05.320
"Is that a f---in' Bible?"

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:07.860
"Hey, the Holy f---in' Bible, son."

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:09.200
Why is this important?

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:14.800
Well, aside from answering man's most fundamental
questions about nature, being, and the nature

00:01:14.810 --> 00:01:19.219
of existence, it sets the stage nicely for
two stoners to meet at a convenience store

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:21.020
in New Jersey in the 1970s.

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:22.400
The place?

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:27.200
The unincorporated community of Leonardo,
New Jersey, just outside the Quick Stop.

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:27.900
The time?

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:29.200
The 1970s.

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:32.300
What is about to occur is nothing short of
destiny.

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:35.220
"What the hell?

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:37.540
Excuse me, who's watching these babies?"

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:40.060
"The fat one's watching the little one."

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:45.680
Just like that, Jay and Silent Bob were united,
hetero life-mates from the cradle to the grave.

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:49.920
Also, did you know Kevin Smith's daughter
is playing baby Silent Bob?

00:01:50.180 --> 00:01:51.400
It's her screen debut.

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:52.460
It's adorable.

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:58.300
That's right, savages, the second movie in
the Askewniverse takes place before the first.

00:01:58.500 --> 00:01:59.500
Here's how you can tell:

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:04.600
Most of Mallrats revolves around a dating
game show, run by Michael Rooker's character

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:06.460
machiavellian Jared Svenning.

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:11.880
After tragedy strikes the original contestant,
Svenning's daughter Brandi is forced to replace

00:02:11.890 --> 00:02:13.820
her on the game show at the last minute.

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:16.480
“My dad’s asked me to help him with his
new show.”

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:18.400
“What, like his assistant?”

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:20.040
“As a contestant.”

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:21.900
“You mean that dating game ripoff thing?!

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:23.400
That IS what you’re talking about here,
right?”

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:26.180
The original contestant is named Julie Dwyer.

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:31.400
Wanting to look skinny for the cameras, she
goes on an ill-advised exercise binge at the

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:36.180
YMCA pool, unexpectedly dying of a brain embolism
in the process.

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:40.670
This disaster triggers the plot of Mallrats,
with the boyfriend of Svenning's daughter,

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:46.320
Quint, and his friend Brodie ending up in
a cartoonish farce with Jay and Silent Bob

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:48.980
at the local mall, where the game show is
being shot.

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:53.820
In the end, Quint wins over his girlfriend,
Ben Affleck goes to jail, and we're promised

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:56.760
that Jay and SIlent Bob will get an orangutan
someday.

00:02:57.180 --> 00:02:57.940
And they will.

00:02:58.140 --> 00:02:58.920
Just not yet.

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:02.020
This brings us to Clerks, Kevin Smith's first
movie.

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:07.790
In this film, Quick Stop employee Dante and
his pal Randal attend Julie Dwyer's wake,

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:10.640
placing the movie directly after the events
of Mallrats.

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:14.160
It's like the Indiana Jones movies, but with
more pot.

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:19.570
Clerks introduced the world to Jay and Silent
Bob, scumbag supporting characters who serve

00:03:19.570 --> 00:03:23.480
as counterpoints to the main characters' dour
minimum wage existence.

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:27.520
They also served as founts of wisdom and a
stoner Greek chorus.

00:03:27.860 --> 00:03:31.400
Jay and Silent Bob spend the majority of Clerks
doing what they do best.

00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:36.040
They hang out in front of the Quick Stop,
slinging drugs while Jay makes noise and Bob

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:36.620
doesn't.

00:03:37.240 --> 00:03:42.180
At first glance, the romantic comedy Chasing
Amy doesn't feel like a Jay and Silent Bob

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:45.280
story at all with no snoochies nor boochies
to be found.

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:46.640
This is a movie about love.

00:03:47.180 --> 00:03:52.060
Smith mainstays Ben Affleck and Jason Lee
play creative partners on a comic book series

00:03:52.060 --> 00:03:57.220
titled Bluntman and Chronic, which details
the lives and adventures of two vigilante

00:03:57.220 --> 00:04:01.680
stoners, one lithe, loud, and obnoxious, the
other portly and less verbal.

00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:07.280
They are, of course, based on Jay and Silent
Bob, who Ben Affleck's character, Holden,

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:11.340
goes to meet at a diner to pay them their
royalties for their likeness rights.

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:15.860
There, Silent Bob delivers his biggest speech
to date, giving the movie its title.

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:19.120
"You're Chasing Amy."

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:24.380
He also reveals an unprecedented number of
details about his own personal life, including

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:26.280
a lifelong desire to be a dancer.

00:04:26.680 --> 00:04:30.500
But there's more backstory to this scene than
the movies even fill you in on.

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:35.760
Before they go to meet Holden, Jay and Silent
Bob crash in the living room of Mallrats character

00:04:35.770 --> 00:04:40.960
Trish Jones, sister to Chasing Amy's Allyssa
Jones, in a story that connects the stoners'

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:43.360
arc from Mallrats to the movies that follow.

00:04:43.980 --> 00:04:49.080
A four-issue comic book miniseries, Chasing
Dogma, bridges the gap between Chasing Amy

00:04:49.090 --> 00:04:53.670
and Dogma, finally answering the question
"Hey, what do you think Jay and Bob were doing

00:04:53.670 --> 00:04:54.840
around 1998?"

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:58.520
"Smoking weed, drinking beers, doing coke,
drinking beers, drinking beers beers beers,

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:03.280
rolling fatties, smoking blunts, who smokes
the blunts?

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:04.740
We smoke the blunts"

00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:09.420
Here's the basic synopsis: after Jay gets
the two of them thrown out of Trish's house,

00:05:09.430 --> 00:05:13.850
the duo heads to the mall's department store
to watch John Hughes movies on VHS.

00:05:13.850 --> 00:05:17.700
They get in a fight, then get kicked out of
the RST Video parking lot.

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:22.540
They they head to Shermer, Illinois to try
and sell weed to the Brat Pack characters,

00:05:22.540 --> 00:05:27.460
then get verbally assaulted by Mister Rogers,
eventually landing work on the set of an adult

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:31.340
film directed by Neil Patrick Harris called
Doogie Nights, and that's all in the first

00:05:31.340 --> 00:05:31.840
two issues.

00:05:32.360 --> 00:05:37.460
In a weird twist, issue three explores their
adoption of an escaped orangutan and subsequent

00:05:37.460 --> 00:05:41.820
scrapes with a federal wildlife marshal, which
will sound familiar to some.

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:47.160
Yes, that particular storyline from Jay and
Silent Bob Strike Back apparently happened

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:47.660
twice.

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:52.560
At the end of the run, Jay and Bob discover
that there is no Shermer, Illinois, and decide

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:56.800
to bury their disappointment by heading to
a family planning clinic to meet women.

00:05:57.060 --> 00:05:58.580
They're nothing if not consistent.

00:05:59.240 --> 00:06:03.560
Theologically speaking, everything sort of
comes to a head for New Jersey's favorite

00:06:03.570 --> 00:06:09.440
unlicensed herbal peddlers in 1999, when,
while cruising at the clinic, they meet Bethany

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:13.960
Sloane, the last descendant of a genetic line
shared by Jesus Christ.

00:06:14.420 --> 00:06:18.560
This is the movie in which Jay and Bob are
revealed to be prophets sent by God, which

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:21.340
still isn't "ironic," though it is amusing.

00:06:21.620 --> 00:06:26.230
Jay and Bob escort Bethany on an interstate
journey of self-discovery and heavy religious

00:06:26.230 --> 00:06:26.840
introspection.

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:33.850
Along the way, they befriend Rufus, the secret
13th apostle, and Serendipity, a muse responsible

00:06:33.850 --> 00:06:37.960
for most of history's most financially successful
box office performances.

00:06:38.140 --> 00:06:43.680
Silent Bob proves to be a remarkably effective
demon slayer, defeating two actual demons

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:45.100
over the course of the adventure.

00:06:45.490 --> 00:06:50.560
Jay has less success, and his attempts to
kill a fallen angel with an Uzi mostly make

00:06:50.560 --> 00:06:51.220
things worse.

00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:55.900
Still, through offhand remarks, he takes a
potential end of the world scenario off the

00:06:55.910 --> 00:07:00.600
burner and helps to save God from a comatose
state incurred during one of the Almighty's

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:02.720
trips down to Earth to play skeeball.

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:08.350
Bethany immaculately conceives a holy child,
and according to Kevin Smith, that's all we'll

00:07:08.350 --> 00:07:09.340
be hearing on the matter.

00:07:10.060 --> 00:07:15.111
After four movies and various side projects
in the supporting cast, 2001's Jay and Silent

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:17.440
Bob Strike Back put the pair center stage.

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:23.420
The movie sees the duo learning two important
things: one, Hollywood is adapting Bluntman

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:27.750
and Chronic into a big budget blockbuster,
and they deserve a cut of the royalties.

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:31.340
Two, the internet exists, and people are mean
there.

00:07:31.560 --> 00:07:35.780
"We gotta put a stop to these f---in hateful
sons of b----es before they ruin our good

00:07:35.780 --> 00:07:36.280
names."

00:07:36.500 --> 00:07:40.400
The two head off to Hollywood to try and shut
down the movie, or at least get paid their

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:42.060
share for their likenesses.

00:07:42.350 --> 00:07:46.880
Along the way, they befriend a quartet of
female jewel thieves masquerading as animal

00:07:46.880 --> 00:07:51.770
rights activists, and are conned into stealing
an orangutan from an animal testing facility

00:07:51.770 --> 00:07:53.420
as part of an elaborate coverup.

00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:55.800
Bob and the ape become dear friends.

00:07:56.320 --> 00:08:00.540
Jay falls in love with one of the criminals,
and Will Ferrell appears as a Will Ferrell

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:01.040
character.

00:08:01.570 --> 00:08:06.160
The jewel thieves are arrested after Justice,
the member of the group who garnered Jay's

00:08:06.169 --> 00:08:11.270
affections, turns them in to save Jay and
Bob from going down for a crime they didn't

00:08:11.270 --> 00:08:11.760
commit.

00:08:12.040 --> 00:08:14.860
She asks Jay to wait for her while she's incarcerated.

00:08:15.080 --> 00:08:20.610
Jay and Bob confront Banky Edwards, the co-creator
of Bluntman and Chronic played by Jason Lee,

00:08:20.610 --> 00:08:25.450
and walk away with a cherry cut of the proceeds
from the forthcoming feature film, leaving

00:08:25.450 --> 00:08:28.060
them financially solvent for the foreseeable
future.

00:08:28.600 --> 00:08:33.840
Shockingly, in the years between Jay and Silent
Bob Strike Back and Clerks II, the beloved

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:35.500
Quick Stop burned to the ground.

00:08:35.880 --> 00:08:38.780
Our boys aren't to blame, though — they
were in rehab at the time.

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:43.000
As chronicled by Jay during his first day
back at work, they bought a car, but were

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:46.480
pulled over for suspicion of mischief, also
known as

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:48.680
"Driving around with a deployed airbag.”

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:54.040
The police found marijuana in their vehicle
and the dynamic duo was sentenced to six months

00:08:54.040 --> 00:08:54.680
of rehab.

00:08:55.100 --> 00:08:58.720
Back on the outside, they continued dealing
drugs, but stopped using.

00:08:59.060 --> 00:09:03.440
They also seemingly picked their business
venue based solely on where Dante and Randal

00:09:03.440 --> 00:09:07.760
were working at the time, setting up shop
in front of a Mooby's fast food restaurant.

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:10.640
They keep to themselves in the background
for the most part.

00:09:10.640 --> 00:09:15.660
Silent Bob achieves his dance dreams in a
sequence of heightened reality, and the two

00:09:15.660 --> 00:09:20.210
are arrested again during a madcap comedy
of errors surrounding a donkey show put on

00:09:20.210 --> 00:09:21.040
inside the restaurant.

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:26.740
After everyone gets taken to jail, the two
offer to finance Dante and Randal's reclamation

00:09:26.740 --> 00:09:31.080
of the rebuilt Quick Stop in exchange for
a permanent residency in front of the store.

00:09:31.540 --> 00:09:33.940
As the credits roll, a line of text reads

00:09:34.400 --> 00:09:36.480
"Jay and Silent Bob might return someday.

00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:38.280
Until then, they're taking it easy."

00:09:38.740 --> 00:09:42.220
Fans speculated as to whether or not they'd
ever see their heroes again.

00:09:42.500 --> 00:09:43.600
13 years passed.

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:44.660
And then...

00:09:45.280 --> 00:09:49.880
After a decade-long career detour with the
studio comedies Zack and Miri Make a Porno

00:09:49.880 --> 00:09:55.000
and Cop Out, as well as a dark horror phase
centered on the great white north of Canada,

00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:59.160
Kevin Smith decided he was ready to go back
to the View Askewniverse.

00:09:59.400 --> 00:10:03.200
The return is officially kicking off in October
2019.

00:10:03.500 --> 00:10:06.400
Remember the plot of Jay and Silent Bob Strike
Back?

00:10:06.620 --> 00:10:11.400
Kevin Smith has described the sequel as being
basically the same movie, even comparing it

00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:14.360
to director Gus Van Sant's shot-for-shot Psycho
remake.

00:10:14.460 --> 00:10:15.980
"Where we taking it from, Gus?"

00:10:19.280 --> 00:10:20.140
"I'm busy."

00:10:20.560 --> 00:10:21.540
"You're a true artist, Gus."

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:26.480
The movie will follow Jay and Silent Bob as
they try to stop a big-budget Hollywood remake

00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:29.660
of the movie they tried to put a stop to in
Strike Back.

00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:34.620
A ton of Smith regulars make appearances,
including Ben Affleck, Jason Lee, and Shannon

00:10:34.630 --> 00:10:39.890
Elizabeth, reprising her role as Justice,
who introduces Jay to their love child Millie,

00:10:39.890 --> 00:10:43.140
played by Kevin Smith's kid, Harley Quinn
Smith.

00:10:43.420 --> 00:10:45.740
She's less adorable this time around, though.

00:10:45.820 --> 00:10:47.520
This time, she means business.

00:10:47.820 --> 00:10:52.440
"Either you take us both to Hollywood or I
stab you to death on my front f---ing lawn."

00:10:52.680 --> 00:10:54.300
Well, like father, like kid.

00:10:54.720 --> 00:10:56.720
